#!/bin/sh
# Started by the openvm-clipdesk service once X answers: the XFCE session of the
# unprivileged guest user. The host owns sleep and blanking (the same reason
# Windows guests have their display timeout off), so X never does either.
export DISPLAY=:99
echo "openvm-desktop: waiting for X"
# timeout: a wedged server accepts the connection and never answers.
i=0
until timeout 3 xset q >/dev/null 2>&1; do
    i=$((i + 1))
    if [ "$i" -ge 10 ]; then
        echo "openvm-desktop: X never answered; its log ends:"
        tail -25 /var/log/Xorg.99.log 2>&1 | sed 's/^/openvm-desktop: /'
        exit 1
    fi
    sleep 1
done
xset s off -dpms
echo "openvm-desktop: input devices:"
xinput list --name-only 2>&1 | sed 's/^/openvm-desktop:   /'

uid=$(id -u openvm)
mkdir -p "/run/user/$uid"
chown openvm:openvm "/run/user/$uid"
chmod 700 "/run/user/$uid"
exec su -s /bin/sh openvm -c "
    export DISPLAY=:99 XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/$uid HOME=/home/openvm
    /usr/local/bin/openvm-clipboard-session
    exec dbus-launch --exit-with-session sh -c 'echo \"\$DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS\" >/run/user/$uid/openvm-bus; exec xfce4-session'
"
